  "definition": "Notable model entries by developer-organization region and publication year. Each source model counted once per region, even with several associated countries there. Cross-region models count in each associated region; totals are not additive global market shares.",
  "geographyNote": "Northern America uses UN M49 subregion 021: US, Canada, Greenland, Bermuda and Saint Pierre and Miquelon. Mexico, Central America, the Caribbean and South America are classified as Latin America and the Caribbean, outside the primary three-region comparison. Europe is not the EU and includes the UK. Editorial exception to M49: Russia is a separate transcontinental category, excluded from both Europe and Asia because source organization-country labels cannot locate developers on either side of the Urals. T\u00fcrkiye and Cyprus are in Asia. Taiwan source labels assigned to Asia as a documented extension to the M49 country table. Unknown or Multinational-only labels are not assigned by guesswork.",
